      en: "The Tokyo National Museum (TNM) in Ueno Park is Japan's largest and oldest museum, founded in 1872. Its comprehensive collection spans Japanese art, archaeology, and Asian artifacts, with over 110,000 items including 89 National Treasures. The main Honkan building, completed in 1938, features a distinctive Japanese modernist style. The museum also includes the Toyokan (Asian art), Hyokeikan (archaeology), and Heiseikan (special exhibitions). Notable exhibits include samurai armor, ukiyo-e prints, and Horyuji temple treasures. The museum plays a vital role in preserving Japan's cultural heritage and promotes international exchange through its research and exhibition programs.",
