      en: "Kintai Bridge in Iwakuni, Yamaguchi Prefecture, is a historic wooden arch bridge built in 1673. Its unique five-arch design, using no nails, showcases traditional Japanese carpentry. The bridge spans 193.3 meters across the Nishiki River. Originally constructed for the daimyo's access to Iwakuni Castle, it was destroyed by a typhoon in 1950 and meticulously rebuilt. The current structure dates from 1953. The bridge is a National Important Cultural Property. It is illuminated at night and is a popular spot for cherry blossom viewing. The nearby Kikko Park offers views of the bridge and surrounding mountains.",
